## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/udimpack.html
- Summary (EN): Takes one input and samples it at several UDIM tiles, packaging the samples into a cable, a Copernicus data type that carries multiple layers. Added in Houdini 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud échantillonne son entrée sur plusieurs tuiles UDIM et regroupe les résultats dans un câble, nœud disponible depuis Houdini 22.0.

- Inputs meaning: ["Single input: the source sampled at each UDIM tile. The node has no input ordering."]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "UDIMs", "meaning": "List of UDIM tiles to sample, comma-separated, with hyphens for ranges. If this list is not enabled, the node uses the default UDIM list from the COP Network."}, {"name": "Add UDIM As", "meaning": "Adds the UDIM number to the output name as a Prefix or a Suffix."}]

- Caveats: ["The page does not describe how UDIM numbers are formatted in the names, how the input is sampled at each tile, or how invalid or out-of-range entries are handled.", "Time Pack is listed as a related node. It works similarly, but across times instead of UDIM tiles."]

